WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.237
-The White House has been rocked
yet again my anonymous warnings

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.105
about the President's
fitness for office,

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.308
and yet Republicans
are still moving forward

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.675
with his Supreme Court pick.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:12.378
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:16.615
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.884
Trump is being allowed
to fill a lifetime seat

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:21.154
to the nation's highest court
despite constant leaks

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.755
about how dangerous
and erratic he is.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.959
Every day, new details emerge
from famed journalist

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.960
Bob Woodward's
upcoming book "Fear,"

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.596
whose cover looks like
a lifetime movie poster

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.098
about an evil stepfather.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.566
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.334
And those details
confirm that Trump

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:39.204
is as vulgar and petulant
in private as he is in public.

00:00:39.204 --> 00:00:40.874
In the book,
even his own aides

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.842
describe Trump
as an "unhinged idiot"

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.377 line:0%
and "professional liar"
who "acted like,

00:00:45.377 --> 00:00:47.780
and had the understanding
of, a fifth- or sixth-grader."

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.948
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.017
Of course, you don't need
a book to know that.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:54.721
You just need eyeballs
and ear holes.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.423
Trump is in private exactly
who he seems to be in public.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:00.360
It's both shocking and not
surprising at the same time.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.062
I mean,
the guy literally misspelled

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.064
his own wife's name in a tweet.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.332
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.235
Not like he's doing that
in public, and then, in private,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.438
besting world leaders
in games of chess.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:14.573
"Bad news, Angela.
It seems you've failed

00:01:14.573 --> 00:01:17.343
to counteract my queen's gambit
by taking my pawn.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.745
And now my knight
has your king in check.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:21.180
So, if you'll excuse me,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.417
I have to meet my wife...
Melanoma?"

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.585
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:29.822
Now, one of the most
eye-catching allegations

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.658
in the book
is that Trump's closest aides

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.194
have resorted
to hiding documents from him

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.962
to stop him
from signing or reading them.

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:40.233
-Woodward describes
an administrative coup d'etat

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.702
and a nervous breakdown
of the executive branch,

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.872
with senior aides conspiring
to pluck official papers

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:49.875
from the President's desk so he
couldn't see or even sign them.

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:52.878
-Woodward also details
the actions of some top aides

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:56.382
in the White House, including
former economic adviser,

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:59.151
Goldman Sachs veteran
Gary Cohn.

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:01.454
"According to Woodward,
Cohn 'stole a letter

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.522
off Trump's desk'
that the President

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:06.492
was intending to go sign
to formally withdraw the U.S.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.695
from a trade agreement
with South Korea."

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.831
-Porter consulted Cohn --
Gary Cohn -- who told him,

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:15.434
according to Woodward,
"I can stop this.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:18.504
I'll just take the paper
off his desk."

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.840
-Craziest thing about
that story is that

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.542
if you steal a piece of paper
from Trump's desk,

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:25.178
he won't even know it's gone.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.846
He's like a guy who's blown away

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.148
by the first half
of a magic trick.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.751
"Oh, my God! How did you get
that lady inside the box?!"

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.320
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.322
This isn't even the first time

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.956
there's been
an explosive allegations

00:02:37.956 --> 00:02:40.092
from a tell-all book about how
the Trump White House

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:41.361
deals with paper.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.429
You might remember that,
just a few weeks ago,

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.898
former Trump aide
Omarosa Manigault Newman

00:02:45.898 --> 00:02:48.468
wrote in her book
that she once saw Trump

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.837
eat paper in the Oval Office.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.139
Now, in fairness,
maybe he was just eating it

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.807
so Gary Cohn
couldn't steal it first.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.008
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:57.076
Gary comes in late at night,
looking for it,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:00.246
and then,
Trump flips on a light and says,

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.248
"Oh, are you looking
for your paper, Gary?"

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.949
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:06.519
"Because I'm afraid I put it
somewhere safe -- my belly."

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.786
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:09.088
"Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.590
I have to meet my wife...
Mallorca?"

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.960
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.831
But the book...

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.800
The book is also filled
with stories from Trump aides

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.670
who have loyally served him and
agreed with most of his agenda,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.938
trying to cast themselves
as heroic saviors

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:28.073
protecting the public
from the whims of a madman.

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:30.109
For example,
Cohn threatened to resign

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.911
after Trump's comments
on Charlottesville.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.914
But Trump "persuaded his
economic adviser to stay on."

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.029
Man, I would've loved
to see that conversation.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.398
"I'm gonna shove this
resignation letter up your ass."

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.400
"Oh, yeah? Well, I'm gonna
shove it in my mouth,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.002
and it'll end up
in the same place."

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.004
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.805
Second, it's easy to talk tough,

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:01.774
but unless you're actually
willing to resign

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.943
and tell the American people
everything you know,

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.844
then your tough talk
is worthless.

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:07.780
John Kelly's like a kid
who tells his friends

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.116
he's gonna stand up to the bully
who steals his lunch money,

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.285
and then, when lunchtime comes,
tells the bully,

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.687
"Keep shaking!
There's more in my back pocket!"

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.222
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.890
Now, Trump has denied
all of this,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.292
and yesterday
in the Oval Office,

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.193
he called Woodward's book
"a work of fiction,"

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:23.296
but that's not what
he told Woodward on the phone

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.031
when he called him
just a few weeks ago

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.333
to complain that he hadn't been
interviewed for the book.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.067
Woodward recorded the call,

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:31.337
and Trump
was very complimentary.

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:02.167
Oh, my God. How is there
always a secret tape

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.070
that contradicts
everything Trump says?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.304
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:06.639
Although I guess
I shouldn't be surprised

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.174
the same guy
who can be tricked into

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.475
not signing a piece of paper

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:10.910
doesn't realize
everyone around him

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.945
has a GoPro
strapped to their heads.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.347
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.348
But, hey,
in fairness to Trump

00:05:16.348 --> 00:05:19.819
he probably didn't know
he was being recorded.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:28.027
-Oh, my God.
He's like a --

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:34.233
[ Applause ]

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:37.170
He's like a bank robber who
waves at the security camera.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.004
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:42.041
Craziest part of this phone call
is when Trump explains

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.943
that his aides never asked him

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.011
if he wanted to do
an interview with Woodward

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:48.514
because they were too afraid.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.382
-So to recap,
Trump says Bob Woodward's book

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:26.085
is a work of fiction because
he never spoke to Woodward

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.353
because his aides
were too afraid to talk to him

00:06:28.353 --> 00:06:30.723
about doing an interview
for Woodward's book,

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.459
which is literally
called "Fear."

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:34.960
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.029
Trump is such a bad liar,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:40.166
even his lies
prove that he's lying.

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:42.268
"Your book called 'Fear'
is totally inaccurate,

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:43.569
and I would've told you that

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:46.772
if my aides weren't too afraid
to come talk to me.

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:47.873
Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:49.741
I have to meet my wife,
Mesothelioma."

00:06:49.741 --> 00:06:51.877
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:54.012
"That's it.
I got to write that down.

00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:57.116
That's definitely it."

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.752
For almost two years, we've had
this frustrating spectacle

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:01.954
of Trump's closest aides
anonymously warning us

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:04.190
that the president they work for
is erratic and dangerous

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.092
but refusing to actually
do anything about it,

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.894
and yesterday, we got the most
stunning example of that yet

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:11.264
from an anonymous op-ed
in "The New York Times," titled

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:12.397
"I Am Part of the Resistance

00:07:12.397 --> 00:07:13.932
Inside the Trump
Administration,"

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:16.735
Warning about Trump's erratic
and reckless behavior.

00:07:16.735 --> 00:07:18.437
And now the op-ed
has put Trump supporters

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:20.172
in the weird position
of having to defend

00:07:20.172 --> 00:07:21.407
the President's mental health,

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:23.275
like South Carolina Senator
Lindsey Graham,

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:26.145
who said this Wednesday on CNN.

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:29.515
-To those who believe
that this man is a fool,

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.484
that this man is crazy,

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:33.619
that there's something wrong
with Donald Trump

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:36.288
and it's just the people around
him that keep us safe,

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:38.524
you don't know
what you're talking about.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:41.160
-Yeah, if you're out there
saying Trump's a kook

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.862
or he's crazy
or he's unfit for office,

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:46.032
you don't know
what you're talking about.

00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:48.701
-I think he's a kook.
I think he's crazy.

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.703
I think he's unfit for office.

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:51.904
-Oh, my God!

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:55.074
The author of the op-ed
was Lindsey Graham!

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:57.977
That would explain the paragraph
where he calls Trump

00:07:57.977 --> 00:08:00.446
crazier than a wet mule eating
corn through a picket fence.

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:02.748
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:04.816
But this week has been
a perfect distillation

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:06.652
of the GOP's complicity
in the Trump debacle,

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:09.621
because even as a parade
of Trump officials

00:08:09.621 --> 00:08:11.890
quietly warn the public
that he's unfit for office,

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.459
they're letting him hang around

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.561
to fill a lifetime seat
on the Supreme Court

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.530
with his handpicked nominee
Brett Kavanaugh.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.097
And in his
confirmation hearing so far,

00:08:19.097 --> 00:08:20.265
Kavanaugh has been exactly

00:08:20.265 --> 00:08:22.267
the kind of loyal partisan
Trump would want.

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:24.136
For example, he's been asked
a series of questions

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:25.905
that could be crucial
to the Russia investigation,

00:08:25.905 --> 00:08:28.073
like "Can the president
pardon himself?"

00:08:28.073 --> 00:08:29.876
"Does he have to comply
with a subpoena?"

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:31.544
And every time,
he has refused to answer

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:33.179
even those basic questions.

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:37.750
-President Trump claims

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.952
he has an absolute right
to pardon himself.

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:42.455
Does he?

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:46.992
-The question of self-pardons is
something I've never analyzed.

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:48.661
-Can a sitting President

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:51.897
be required to respond
to a subpoena?

00:08:51.897 --> 00:08:54.433
-So that's
a hypothetical question.

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:55.601
-No, it's not.

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:57.703
The president's lawyer,
Rudy Giuliani,

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.372
is on TV every day
talking about how Trump

00:09:00.372 --> 00:09:01.907
would just ignore a subpoena.

00:09:01.907 --> 00:09:03.809
You know, this guy.
Always looked like

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:07.312
he just had a resignation letter
shoved up his ass.

00:09:07.312 --> 00:09:09.281
I mean, it's mind-boggling

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:11.350
that we're even considering
allowing the President

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:13.185
to fill a lifetime seat
on the Supreme Court

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:14.687
while his own aides
warn the public

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:15.954
that he's unfit for office.

00:09:15.954 --> 00:09:18.290
But that's the corrupt bargain
the GOP has made.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.892
They're not heroes
containing Trump.

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.327
They're collaborators
working with him

00:09:21.327 --> 00:09:22.761
even though they know he's...

00:09:22.761 --> 00:09:23.763
-A kook.

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.598
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:29.201
[ Cheers and applause ]

